Allow an explicit per-model mem_fraction_static in SparkStation.

The launcher derives mem-fraction from memory_gb and hard-clamps it at 0.82:

    mem_fraction = min(memory_gb / 119.0, 0.82)

so raising memory_gb alone cannot go higher. The clamp's comment records 0.88
hanging a node "only recoverable by unplugging". That predates the NVFP4
lm_head fix in the dflash2 image — the dense dequant at draft-graph capture was
the original reboot cause — and the upstream recipe validates 0.90 on the
patched image. 0.90 booted clean here.

This adds an `extra_args.mem_fraction_static` override, still bounded at 0.92,
with `docker_memory_gb` left as the cgroup backstop so the container OOMs
before the node does. The derived path is unchanged when no override is set.

Worth knowing before you use it: mem-fraction measured as a NULL result for
throughput here. 0.82 / 0.85 / 0.90 all land within run-to-run noise, because
concurrency is bound by mamba slots and long context by prefill, not by memory
capacity. See results/RESULTS.md. The override exists for headroom and for
co-hosting, not for speed.

Apply from the sparkstation repo root:

    git apply /path/to/sparkstation-mem-fraction-override.patch

Then set it on a model in models.yaml:

    extra_args:
      mem_fraction_static: 0.85

A full restart is required — the supervisor imports the launcher, so a
model-only restart will not pick up the change.

--- a/supervisor/launchers/sglang_launcher.py
+++ b/supervisor/launchers/sglang_launcher.py
@@
                 # Calculate mem_fraction_static from allocated memory_gb, with a
                 # SAFETY CLAMP: never exceed 0.82 on unified memory (see the
                 # wedge note above; 0.88 hung the node, 0.78 booted clean).
-                if memory_gb is not None:
+                # Explicit per-model override wins over the derived value. The
+                # 0.82 clamp below predates the NVFP4 lm_head fix in the dflash2
+                # image (the dense-dequant at draft-graph capture was what took
+                # nodes down); the upstream recipe validates 0.90 on that image.
+                # Still bounded at 0.92, and docker_memory_gb remains the
+                # cgroup backstop so the container OOMs before the node does.
+                override = config.extra_args.get("mem_fraction_static")
+                if override is not None:
+                    mem_fraction = min(float(override), 0.92)
+                    logger.info(f"Using mem_fraction_static={mem_fraction:.3f} (explicit override, capped ≤0.92)")
+                    docker_cmd.extend(["--mem-fraction-static", str(mem_fraction)])
+                elif memory_gb is not None:
                     mem_fraction = min(memory_gb / 119.0, 0.82)
                     logger.info(f"Using mem_fraction_static={mem_fraction:.3f} (from {memory_gb}GB, clamped ≤0.82)")
                     docker_cmd.extend(["--mem-fraction-static", str(mem_fraction)])
